<!doctype linuxdoc system>

<article>

<!-- Title information -->

<title>Isearch
<author>Archibald Warnock <htmlurl url="mailto:awww@home.com"
  name="awww@home.com">, A/WWW Enterprises
<date>v1.41, 15 May 1998

<!-- Begin the document -->
<p>
<verb>
Isearch -d dbname [-V][-p X][-q][-t][-and][-rpn][-infix][-prefix X][-suffix X][-byterange][-startdoc X][-enddoc X][-o opt][-RECT{N S E W}] expression
</verb>

<p>

<descrip>
<tag/[-d (X)]/ Search database with root name (X)
<tag/[-V]/ Print the version number.
<tag/[-p (X)]/Present element set (X) with results.
<tag/[-q]/Print results and quit immediately.
<tag/[-t]/Print terse results and quit immediately.
<tag/[-and]/Perform boolean "and" on results.
<tag/[-rpn]/Interpret as an RPN query.
<tag/[-infix]/Interpret as a boolean algebra query.
<tag/[-prefix (X)]/Add prefix (X) to matched terms in document.
<tag/[-suffix (X)]/Add suffix (X) to matched terms in document.
<tag/[-byterange]/Print the byte range of each document within the file that contains it.
<tag/[-startdoc (X)]/Display result set starting with the (X)th document in the list.
<tag/[-enddoc (X)]/Display result set ending with the (X)th document in the list.
<tag/[-RECT{North South West East}]/ Find targets that overlap this geographic rectangle.
<tag/[-o (X)]/Document type specific option.
<tag/(X) (Y) (...)/Search for words (X), (Y), etc.
<p>
<itemize>
<item>[fieldname/]searchterm[*][:n]
<item>Prefix with fieldname/ for fielded searching.
<item>Append * for right truncation.
<item>Append :n for term weighting (default=1).
<item>(Use negative values to lower rank.)
</itemize>
</descrip>

<p>
<descrip>
<tag/Examples:/ Isearch -d POETRY truth "beaut*" urn:2
<tag/ /Isearch -d WEBPAGES title/library
<tag/ /Isearch -d STORIES -rpn title/cat title/dog or title/mouse and
<tag/ /Isearch -d STORIES -infix '(title/cat or title/dog) and title/mouse'
<tag/ /Isearch -d PRUFROCK -infix '(ether and table) or mermaids'
<tag/ /Isearch -d BIBLE -infix '(Saul||Goliath)&amp;&amp;David'
</descrip>

</article>






